<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constitution of the United States</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1787">1787</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as US Constitution, United States Constitution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> was drafted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-convention-united-states">Philadelphia Convention</a> in 1787, ratified in 1788 and in force from 1789. It replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/articles-of-confederation">Articles of Confederation</a> with a federal government divided into legislative, executive and judicial branches, each checking the others. The Bill of Rights was added in 1791, and with twenty-seven amendments it is the oldest written national constitution still in use.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states.jpg" alt="Constitution of the United States" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Constitutional Convention · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Constitution_of_the_United_States_-_DPLA_-_9ca804144bd5965e992ae3528bc3c6a3_(page_1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
